From 9921d54ac41b9975af327578f028b70f935ad28b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:31:35 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 40/43] GE: read a palette texture over a render target on the
 GPU

A game can texture from its own framebuffer through a palette: a CLUT4/8/16/32
texture whose address and row length are a render target's reads the
rendered pixels' bits as indices. One game grades its whole frame this way,
one colour channel per pass through the CLUT index shift and mask. Such a
texture was never matched to its render target, so it was decoded from guest
memory, which holds at best the 1x write-back of an older frame: the effect
drew a flat colour over the screen.

A palette view is now found like any texture over a render target, when its
rows are the target's rows and its index fits a whole number of times in a
pixel, inside the part of the target its draws reached. A pass at the
internal scale (shaders/fb_clut.frag) turns each pixel of the target's copy
back into the guest pixel the GE would hold (5650, 5551, 4444 or 8888, the
top bits of each channel, as the write-back stores them), takes the texel's
index from its bits (the low bits first for indices smaller than a pixel),
applies the CLUT's shift, mask and start, and looks the entry up in the
palette: 512 decoded entries from guest memory, kept per distinct palette,
or the render target the CLUT address lies in, read at the internal scale.
The draw samples that picture as it samples any render target, so the
filtering comes after the lookup. A picture made for a draw recorded for
frame interpolation is kept until no recorded frame can name it, as the
render-target snapshots are; others are reused at once, in command order.

<prefix>_NO_FB_CLUT decodes guest memory, as before. <prefix>_TRACE_FB_CLUT
logs the first 400 palette views with their CLUT, its first entries and the
draw's blend and vertices. The GE census counts them as fbtex.clut_view
(handled) and a CLUT read from a render target as clut.in_target, instead
of fbtex.miss_clut_view and fbtex.format_reinterpreted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
